The Terror of Cagley, which the children of Cagley called the Shadow Demon, is a tall, gangly figure made of cut-out darkness, with two pinprick points of white light for eyes. It laired at the bottom of the mine beneath Mount Cagley, near the town of [[Cagley]]. When the children who had come to kill it reached the bottom, it looked up and said, "I'm so glad you all came."

It shows a victim a death that has succeeded, and the fear of it takes root. It can wear the shape of someone its victim dreads: one child saw it become his football coach, telling him he would never make varsity.

A group of Cagley children destroyed it and escaped the collapsing cavern. The town was left unhaunted. The creature will reform in thirty years.
